kg:note_ref9691_bibliography_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.83, fig.50.\"" .

kg:note_ref9691_odd_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "D-1019" .

kg:note_ref9691_odd_0_p_1 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "FSA A.06 05.1019" .

kg:note_ref9691_odd_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Thomas Leisten's publication, Excavation of Samarra, vol 1." .

kg:note_ref9691_odd_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Drawings related primarly to the first campaign of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin in 1911." .

kg:note_ref9691_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Additional information reads, \"During the relatively short period of work at Manqūr / Balkuwārā in the summer and early fall of 1911, Herzfeld's efforts focused mainly on the central reception block between the third courtyard and the so-called river garden above the Tigris, especially on the eastern Īwān and some adjacent easterly rooms. He surveyed the rest of the reception block of the palace, including the cruciform domed hall in the center as well as the courtyard houses and ancillary complexes with the two maidāns to the south and north and added their general outlines, as far as they were visible among the ruins, to the plan. Herzfeld was certainly interested in the main architectonic features of the palace, but at the same time had hoped to uncover new varieties of stucco wall ornaments and to make major ceramic finds. In both he was disappointed. This probably contributed to his decision to stop the work on the site at the end of September 1911.\" [Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.91.\"]" .

kg:note_ref9691_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Handwritten annotations in German reads, \"Afgenommen (?) von E. Herzfeld.\"" .

kg:note_ref9691_scopecontent_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Handwritten number, probably by Joseph upton, reads, \"D-1019.\"" .

kg:note_ref9691_scopecontent_3_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Additional information from staff reads, \"multiple annotations in English, probably for publication.\"" .

kg:note_ref9691_scopecontent_4_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Additional information from Finding Aid reads, \"Samarra. Plan of unidentified palace. Water-color.\"" .

kg:note_ref9691_scopecontent_5_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Excavation of Samarra (Iraq): Balkuwara Palace: Watercolor Plan [drawing]" .

