kg:note_ref9720_odd_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Drawing related primarly to the archaeological expedition along the Euphrates and Tigris valleys, carried out by Ernst Herzfeld and Friedrich Sarre from October 1907 and March 1908 or the first campaign of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin in 1911." .

kg:note_ref9720_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Original caption reads, \"Samarra, Qubbat al-Sulaibiyya.\"" .

kg:note_ref9720_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Additional information reads, \"Visiting the site of Samarra in 1908, Sarre and Herzfeld had already become interested in the Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya. Herzfeld published preliminary measurements as well as a tentative interpretation of the building as the mausoleum of three of the caliphs of Samarra in 1911. During his absence at the end of June 1911, after some of his most skilled workmen from Ḥillah had begun to remove the debris in and around the building, Herzfeld returned to the Qubbat al-Ṣulaibiyya in the early days of December 1911. Between December 3 and 5, additional research was undertaken in the form of a deep sounding within the main chamber of the building that revealed three skeletons.\" [Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.72.\"]" .

kg:note_ref9720_scopecontent_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Excavation of Samarra (Iraq): Qubbat al-Sulaibiyya: Ground Plan and Section of the Octagonal Building [drawing]" .

