kg:note_ref9746_odd_2_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Drawings related primarly to the first campaign of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin in 1911." .

kg:note_ref9746_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Additional information reads, \"Herzfeld spent not more than two days during the second campaign in the mosque of al-Mutawakkiliyya (June 19-20, 1913), partially excavating the miḥrāb, and 'scraping' - as he admits himself - at the court facade of the transept and in the qibla aisle of the ḥaram, and finally at the plinth of the minaret. While Herzfeld sketched the overall plan of the Great Mosque complex at Mutawakkiliyya in 1913, the final product is based partially on measurements taken by his surveyor, Commander von Ludloff.\" [Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.58.\"]" .

kg:note_ref9746_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Excavation of Samarra (Iraq): Congregational Mosque of Madinat al-Mutawakkiliyya (Abu Dulaf Mosque): Ground Plan of the Mosque and Ziyada [drawing]" .

