kg:note_ref9756_scopecontent_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Scope and Contents" ;
    crm:P148_has_component kg:note_ref9756_scopecontent_0_p_0 ;
    crm:P2_has_type mbs:ScopeContent ;
    rdf:value "Scope and Contents Original handwritten notes reads, \"Haus VI (and VII); Haus VI; VIa; VIIa; Haus V; Haus VII. Samarra. unpublished. (from sketch book).\"" ;
    mbs:noteType mbs:ScopeContent .

kg:note_ref9756_scopecontent_1 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Scope and Contents" ;
    crm:P148_has_component kg:note_ref9756_scopecontent_1_p_0 ;
    crm:P2_has_type mbs:ScopeContent ;
    rdf:value "Scope and Contents The identification of the residential sites: \"Herzfeld numbered all sites while the excavation was still in progress. When it became obvious that two courtyards with adjacent rooms turned out to belong to the same complex, however, he assigned new numbers. Herzfeld gave numbers to 16 houses in various locations, splitting certain buildings, [...] naming in all 24 different sites. [...]. Unfortunately, Herzfeld changed the numbering of the houses a third time when he finished the final drawings for the publication, including only 14 houses. [...]. In those cases in which Herzfeld noted on his field sketch either the name of the area or the new numbering of the house we can at least identify the site.\" [Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003; p.121.\"]" ;
    mbs:noteType mbs:ScopeContent .

