    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Drawings are arranged roughly in sequential number sequences, housed in document boxes or in flat file folders by size, and stored in the map case drawers.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note Transliteration on drawing paper related primarly to the excavation of Persepolis, initiated by Ernst Herzfeld in early March 1931, under the auspices of the Oriental Institute of the University of Chicago. Herzfeld left Persepolis permanently in Spring 1934.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Ernst Herzfeld original drawing's caption and Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers D-1303 FSA A.06 05.1303",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten annotation in German, probably for publication, reads, \".\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten caption in German reads, \"Dar. Pers. c.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten number in red, on verso, reads, \"9.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten numbers, on recto reads, \"top) 5789; bottom) [34].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten signature reads, \"EH.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Sketchbook in Ernst Herzfeld Papers: SK-11, p.1." ;
