        kg:concept_drawings ;
    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Drawings are arranged roughly in sequential number sequences, housed in document boxes or in flat file folders by size, and stored in the map case drawers.",
        "Bibliography Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.59, fig.32.\"",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note Drawings related primarly to the first campaign of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin in 1911.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Thomas Leisten's publication, Excavation of Samarra, vol 1.",
        "Local Numbers D-1083 FSA A.06 05.1083",
        "Scope and Contents Additional information reads, \"Herzfeld spent not more than two days during the second campaign in the mosque of al-Mutawakkiliyya (June 19-20, 1913), partially excavating the miḥrāb, and 'scraping' - as he admits himself - at the court facade of the transept and in the qibla aisle of the ḥaram, and finally at the plinth of the minaret. While Herzfeld sketched the overall plan of the Great Mosque complex at Mutawakkiliyya in 1913, the final product is based partially on measurements taken by his surveyor, Commander von Ludloff.\" [Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.58.\"]",
        "Scope and Contents Excavation of Samarra (Iraq): Congregational Mosque of Madinat al-Mutawakkiliyya (Abu Dulaf Mosque): Ground Plan of the Mosque and Ziyada [drawing]" ;
    crm:P48_has_preferred_identifier kg:id_ark_ref9746 ;
