    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Drawings are arranged roughly in sequential number sequences, housed in document boxes or in flat file folders by size, and stored in the map case drawers.",
        "Bibliography Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.112-114.\"",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note Drawings related primarly to the first campaign of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin in 1911.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Thomas Leisten's publication, Excavation of Samarra, vol 1.",
        "Local Numbers D-1084 FSA A.06 05.1084",
        "Scope and Contents Additional information reads, \"Ṣūr ʿĪṣā belongs to the group of large buildings within the ruin that Herzfeld did not excavate in 1911-1912 for lack of time, though he did make tracings from the remains still visible on the ground.\" [Leisten, Thomas, 2003: \"Excavation of Samarra, v. I. Architecture : Final report of the first campaign 1910-1912. Verlag Philipp von Zabern, Mainz am Rhein, 2003. p.112.\"]",
        "Scope and Contents Excavation of Samarra (Iraq): Sur Isa, Identified as al-Mutawakkil's Palace of al-Burj [drawing]" ;
