    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement - Journals, letters, and sketchbooks are arranged roughly in sequential number sequences, housed in document boxes.",
        "Arrangement - S-11 is organized into 37 subdivisions which include one or several items of original materials.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note Notes related primarly to the two campaigns of excavation at Sāmarrāʼ (Iraq), carried out by Ernst Herzfeld on behalf of the Kaiser Friedrich Museum in Berlin between the years 1911 and 1913.",
        "Existence and Location of Copies - Illustration numbered Orn. 194, Orn. 186b, Orn. 189, Orn. 194, Orn. 199b; reproduced in \"Herzfeld, 1923: Der Wandschmuck der Bauten von Samarra und seine Ornamentik. Berlin, D. Reimer. Plate LXIX, bottom.\"",
        "General - Series title in Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive reads, \"Records of Samarra Expeditions.\"",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive and Thomas Leisten's publication, Excavation of Samarra, vol 1.",
        "Local Numbers S-11 D-1237 FSA A.06 07.11.04 FSA A.06 05.1237",
        "Scope and Contents - Original publication caption for Orn. 186b reads: \"186b. Bemalte Holzleiste IN-875; Djausaq, am quadratischen Hof hinter den Vorsälen.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original publication caption for Orn. 189 reads: \"189a. Bemalte Holzleiste IN-?; Djausaq, am quadratischen Hof hinter den Vorsälen.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original publication caption for Orn. 194 reads: \"194. Bemalte Holzleiste IN-978; Djausaq, basilikale Thronsäle.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original publication caption for Orn. 199b reads: \"199b. Bemalte Holzleiste IN-616; Djausaq, nördl. Räume zwischen Groβem Innenhof und Sardâb.\"",
        "Scope and Contents Excavation of Samarra (Iraq): Typological Study of Painted Decoration on Wood [drawing]" ;
    crm:P48_has_preferred_identifier kg:id_ark_ref9893 ;
