        kg:concept_drawings ;
    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Drawings are arranged roughly in sequential number sequences, housed in document boxes or in flat file folders by size, and stored in the map case drawers.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note Drawing related to a trial excavation undertook by Ernst Herzfeld in the Summer 1928 as well as a campaign of excavation at the western mound, Tall-i-Bakun A under the auspice of the Oriental Institute of the University of Chicago, carried out by Alexander Langsdorff under Ernst Herzfeld's direction between March 25, 1932 and July 21, 1932.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Ernst Herzfeld original drawing's caption and Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers D-405 FSA A.06 05.0405",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten Roman number on verso reads, \"LIII.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten annotation on board reads, \"Tafel XXXIII; 10.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten number, probably by Joseph Upton, reads, \"D-405; D-406.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten signature reads, \"EH.\"",
        "Scope and Contents Excavation of Persepolis (Iran): Reconstruction of Pottery with Painted Patterns: Two Conical Bowls, from Prehistoric Mound of Tal-i Bakun (PPA) [drawing]" ;
    crm:P48_has_preferred_identifier kg:id_ark_ref9103 ;
